---

<section class="idea-section not-content" id="the-idea">
  <div class="idea-container">
    {/* Section 1: The Evolution */}
    <div class="idea-narrative-block">
      <div class="narrative-meta">
        <span class="idea-eyebrow">The Problem &amp; Core Idea</span>
        <h2 class="idea-main-title">Why this engineering handbook is needed</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="narrative-content">
        <p class="lead-text">
          Language models are no longer just text in, text out. We are embedding them into <strong>autonomous agentic systems</strong>: programs where models direct dynamic execution loops, plan multi-step strategies, read persistent memories, and dispatch tools that read databases, execute code, and send API requests.
        </p>
        <p>
          This shift completely breaks traditional software security assumptions. In a standard application, control flow is hardcoded in deterministic code and separated from user data. In an agentic system, <strong>untrusted data can hijack model control flow</strong> and turn the agent's own authorized tools against the host environment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 2: The Three Core Realities */}
    <div class="realities-grid">
      <div class="reality-card">
        <div class="reality-num">01</div>
        <h3 class="reality-heading">Prompt injection is an architectural flaw, not a typo</h3>
        <p class="reality-text">
          You cannot fix prompt injection with prompt engineering or regex filters. Because language models process instructions and retrieved data in the exact same token stream, untrusted data can redirect the agent's intent. Security must be enforced at runtime boundaries, credential scopes, and tool execution gates.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reality-card">
        <div class="reality-num">02</div>
        <h3 class="reality-heading">You cannot secure a system you cannot explain</h3>
        <p class="reality-text">
          Memorizing generic vulnerability lists or OWASP Top 10 badges fails when engineers don't understand how the 5-step agent loop operates, how context windows get packed, how vector stores retrieve memories, or how tool schemas are dispatched. We construct the complete distributed architecture first before attacking it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reality-card">
        <div class="reality-num">03</div>
        <h3 class="reality-heading">Zero hand-waving: grounded in verifiable evidence</h3>
        <p class="reality-text">
          Every assertion, boundary diagram, and defensive recommendation in this handbook is grounded in official RFCs, NIST benchmarks, Model Context Protocol specs, and peer-reviewed research. We link directly to canonical sources and provide small, runnable code tests for each boundary.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 3: The Handbook's Method */}
    <div class="method-banner">
      <div class="method-left">
        <span class="method-label">The Engineering Method</span>
        <h3 class="method-title">Architecture First · Defense in Depth Second</h3>
        <p class="method-desc">
          We teach in strict dependency order: from distributed systems boundaries and autonomous control loops to tool privilege isolation, sandboxed execution runtimes, and automated red team evaluation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="method-features">
        <div class="m-feat">
          <span class="m-dot teal"></span>
          <div>
            <strong>Cartoon System Schemas</strong>
            <span>Intuitive visual mental models that clarify where data flows and where trust boundaries lie.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="m-feat">
          <span class="m-dot amber"></span>
          <div>
            <strong>Runnable Code Examples</strong>
            <span>Verified Python and TypeScript snippets modeling each lifecycle step and security control.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="m-feat">
          <span class="m-dot lavender"></span>
          <div>
            <strong>Machine-Readable AEO &amp; LLMs.txt</strong>
            <span>Structured endpoints so AI search engines and developer agents can cite and retrieve every chapter.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .idea-section {
    width: 100%;
    padding: clamp(4rem, 8vh, 6.5rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4.5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    background-color: var(--color-canvas);
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .idea-container {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(3rem, 6vh, 4.5rem);
  }

  /* Narrative Block */
  .idea-narrative-block {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.95fr) minmax(0, 1.35fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .narrative-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .idea-eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--color-teal);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .idea-main-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.2vw, 3.1rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .narrative-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .narrative-content .lead-text {
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.6vw, 1.32rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .narrative-content p {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.3vw, 1.12rem);
    line-height: 1.72;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .narrative-content strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  /* Realities Grid */
  .realities-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .reality-card {
    background-color: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: 2.25rem 2rem;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 16px -2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.03);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    transition: all 200ms cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .reality-card {
    background-color: var(--color-surface-card);
    border-color: var(--color-border);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 20px -2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
  }

  .reality-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    border-color: var(--color-teal);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 28px -4px var(--color-teal-subtle);
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .reality-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-mauve);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px -4px rgba(203, 166, 247, 0.2);
  }

  .reality-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.85rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--color-teal);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .reality-num {
    color: var(--color-mauve);
  }

  .reality-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  .reality-text {
    font-size: 0.96rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Method Banner */
  .method-banner {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-surface) 0%, var(--color-surface-subtle) 100%);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 20px;
    padding: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.25rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    align-items: center;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px -4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .method-banner {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-surface-card) 0%, var(--color-surface-subtle) 100%);
    border-color: var(--color-border);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 30px -4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }

  .method-label {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--color-teal);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .method-label {
    color: var(--color-mauve);
  }

  .method-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.5vw, 2.1rem);
    font-weight: 750;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .method-desc {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .method-features {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.15rem;
  }

  .m-feat {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .m-dot {
    width: 9px;
    height: 9px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .m-dot.teal { background-color: var(--color-teal); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--color-teal-subtle); }
  .m-dot.amber { background-color: var(--color-amber); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--color-amber-subtle); }
  .m-dot.lavender { background-color: var(--color-lavender); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--color-lavender-subtle); }

  .m-feat div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.2rem;
  }

  .m-feat strong {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .m-feat span {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .idea-narrative-block {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.75rem;
    }

    .realities-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .method-banner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .idea-section {
      padding: 3rem 1rem 4rem;
    }

    .reality-card {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }

    .method-banner {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
